IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-interpretation`
IMPORT `sgf-s216`

-- Tests for sgf-s216.l4 (s 216, personal remedies in cases of oppression or injustice).
-- Every expected value below was written from the text of s 216 (src:21698-21781 of CoA1967.txt) before the module was run,
-- never copied from its output. A failing assertion is a finding. Each rule is tried on both sides of each of its conditions.
-- Positions of the arguments are named in the comment above each group.

§ `s 216(1): who may apply`

-- Arguments, in order: the body is a company incorporated under this Act; ... under a corresponding previous written law;
-- the person is a member; shares transmitted to the person by operation of law; the person holds a debenture; the person is the
-- Minister; the company is a declared company under Part 9; the court applied to is the General Division of the High Court.

-- A member of a company incorporated under the Act, applying to the Court: the text says "Any member ... may apply".
#ASSERT `s 216(1) the person may apply to the Court for an order under this section` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A member of a company incorporated under a corresponding previous written law: "company" in s 4(1) covers it.
#ASSERT `s 216(1) the person may apply to the Court for an order under this section` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A holder of a debenture who is not a member: "or holder of a debenture of a company".
#ASSERT `s 216(1) the person may apply to the Court for an order under this section` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A person who is not a member but to whom shares have been transmitted by operation of law: s 216(7) applies the section to that person.
#ASSERT `s 216(1) the person may apply to the Court for an order under this section` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Minister, in the case of a declared company under Part 9.
#ASSERT `s 216(1) the person may apply to the Court for an order under this section` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Minister of a declared company that is not a "company" under s 4(1) (for instance a foreign company the Minister has declared, Part 9, s 229):
-- the Minister's limb is tied to "a declared company under Part 9" and not to s 4(1) "company" (fork F-216-1), so the Minister may apply.
#ASSERT `s 216(1) the person may apply to the Court for an order under this section` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Minister, where the company is not a declared company under Part 9: outside the limit of the grant; the text does not say.
#ASSERT `s 216(1) the person may apply to the Court for an order under this section` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A person who is none of a member, a transmittee, a holder of a debenture or the Minister: outside the three classes; not covered.
#ASSERT `s 216(1) the person may apply to the Court for an order under this section` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A member of a body that is not a company (neither incorporated under the Act nor under a corresponding previous written law): not covered.
#ASSERT `s 216(1) the person may apply to the Court for an order under this section` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A member who would apply to some court other than the General Division of the High Court: not covered ("may apply to the Court").
#ASSERT `s 216(1) the person may apply to the Court for an order under this section` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A member who is also a debenture holder: still JUST TRUE (the classes are alternatives).
#ASSERT `s 216(1) the person may apply to the Court for an order under this section` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `s 216(7): a person to whom shares have been transmitted by operation of law`

-- Arguments: the person is a member of the company; shares have been transmitted to the person by operation of law.
#ASSERT `s 216(7) the person is treated as a member for the purposes of the section` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(7) the person is treated as a member for the purposes of the section` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(7) the person is treated as a member for the purposes of the section` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 216(1)(a): the first ground (oppression, or disregard of interests)`

-- Arguments, in order: the matter complained of (the s 4(8) list); the corporation is a trustee and is not a trustee corporation;
-- the act or thing was done during a receivership, judicial management, administered arrangement or winding up; the corporation has
-- issued interests; the powers of the directors are being exercised in the manner complained of; the manner is oppressive;
-- the manner is in disregard of interests.

-- Internal management of the company (s 4(8)(c)), conducted oppressively: the affairs limb and the oppression limb both hold.
#ASSERT `s 216(1)(a) the ground is established` `s 4(8)(c) the internal management and proceeding of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same matter, conducted in disregard of interests but not oppressively: "or in disregard of" is an alternative.
#ASSERT `s 216(1)(a) the ground is established` `s 4(8)(c) the internal management and proceeding of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither oppressive nor in disregard: the ground is not made out; the text says no.
#ASSERT `s 216(1)(a) the ground is established` `s 4(8)(c) the internal management and proceeding of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The powers of the directors exercised oppressively: the second conduct limb holds whatever the matter.
#ASSERT `s 216(1)(a) the ground is established` `s 4(8) some other matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A matter off the s 4(8) list, no exercise of the directors' powers, conducted oppressively: s 4(8) is "including", so the list is open: NOT covered, never FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 216(1)(a) the ground is established` `s 4(8) some other matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Beneficiaries under a trust (s 4(8)(b)), where the corporation is a trustee but not a trustee corporation: on the list.
#ASSERT `s 216(1)(a) the ground is established` `s 4(8)(b) the identity of the beneficiaries under a trust of which the corporation is trustee, their rights and the payments they have received or are entitled to receive` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same matter where the corporation is not such a trustee: the paragraph's own condition fails, so NOT covered.
#ASSERT `s 216(1)(a) the ground is established` `s 4(8)(b) the identity of the beneficiaries under a trust of which the corporation is trustee, their rights and the payments they have received or are entitled to receive` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An act done while the corporation was being wound up (s 4(8)(d)(iv)): on the list where the condition holds.
#ASSERT `s 216(1)(a) the ground is established` `s 4(8)(d) an act or thing done by or on behalf of the corporation, or to or in relation to it or its business or property, at a time when it was in receivership, under judicial management, administering a compromise or arrangement, or being wound up` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Matters concerning interests the corporation has issued (s 4(8)(i)): "where the corporation has issued interests"; none issued: NOT covered.
#ASSERT `s 216(1)(a) the ground is established` `s 4(8)(i) the financial or business undertaking, scheme, common enterprise or investment contract to which interests issued by the corporation relate` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216(1)(a) the ground is established` `s 4(8)(i) the financial or business undertaking, scheme, common enterprise or investment contract to which interests issued by the corporation relate` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 4(9) gives the same list for "the affairs of a company": the same matter answers the same way when s 4(9) is asked.
#ASSERT `s 4(9) a reference to the affairs of a company or a foreign company covers the matter` TRUE `s 4(8)(e) the ownership of shares in, debentures of, and interests issued by, the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `s 216(1)(b): the second ground (an act or resolution that discriminates or prejudices)`

-- Arguments: an act of the company has been done or is threatened; a resolution has been passed or is proposed; it unfairly
-- discriminates; it is otherwise prejudicial.
#ASSERT `s 216(1)(b) the ground is established` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(1)(b) the ground is established` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(1)(b) the ground is established` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither an act nor a resolution: no ground, whatever the effect.
#ASSERT `s 216(1)(b) the ground is established` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An act, but it neither discriminates unfairly nor prejudices.
#ASSERT `s 216(1)(b) the ground is established` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 216(1) read with (2): either of the grounds`

-- Arguments: the answer for the ground in paragraph (a); the answer for the ground in paragraph (b).
#ASSERT `s 216(1) either of the grounds is established` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(1) either of the grounds is established` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(1) either of the grounds is established` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 216(1) either of the grounds is established` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(1) either of the grounds is established` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216(1) either of the grounds is established` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 216(2): the Court's order`

-- Arguments: the Court is of the opinion that either ground is established; the order is made with a view to bringing to an end or remedying the matters complained of.
#ASSERT `s 216(2) the Court may make the order it thinks fit` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Court has not formed the opinion: the "if" gate of a grant fails; the text does not say the Court may not.
#ASSERT `s 216(2) the Court may make the order it thinks fit` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The order is not made with that view: outside the purpose the grant states.
#ASSERT `s 216(2) the Court may make the order it thinks fit` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216(2) the Court may make the order it thinks fit` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2)(a) direct or prohibit any act, or cancel or vary any transaction or resolution.
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(a) the order may direct or prohibit any act or cancel or vary any transaction or resolution` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(a) the order may direct or prohibit any act or cancel or vary any transaction or resolution` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(a) the order may direct or prohibit any act or cancel or vary any transaction or resolution` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(b) regulate the conduct of the affairs of the company in future.
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(b) the order may regulate the conduct of the affairs of the company in future` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(b) the order may regulate the conduct of the affairs of the company in future` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(b) the order may regulate the conduct of the affairs of the company in future` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(c) authorise civil proceedings in the name of or on behalf of the company.
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(c) the order may authorise civil proceedings to be brought in the name of or on behalf of the company` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(c) the order may authorise civil proceedings to be brought in the name of or on behalf of the company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(c) the order may authorise civil proceedings to be brought in the name of or on behalf of the company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(f) provide that the company be wound up.
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(f) the order may provide that the company be wound up` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(f) the order may provide that the company be wound up` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(f) the order may provide that the company be wound up` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2)(d) purchase of shares or debentures: the buyer is another member or holder of debentures, or the company itself, or some other person.
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(d) the order may provide for the purchase of the shares or debentures of the company by the buyer` TRUE TRUE `s 216(2)(d) another member or holder of debentures of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(d) the order may provide for the purchase of the shares or debentures of the company by the buyer` TRUE TRUE `s 216(2)(d) the company itself` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Some other buyer: the list names two buyers and is not closed ("without limiting the foregoing"): not covered by (d), never FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(d) the order may provide for the purchase of the shares or debentures of the company by the buyer` TRUE TRUE `s 216(2)(d) some other person` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The "if" gate fails: not covered, for each kind of buyer.
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(d) the order may provide for the purchase of the shares or debentures of the company by the buyer` FALSE TRUE `s 216(2)(d) the company itself` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(d) the order may provide for the purchase of the shares or debentures of the company by the buyer` TRUE FALSE `s 216(2)(d) another member or holder of debentures of the company` EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2)(e) reduction of capital "in the case of a purchase of shares by the company": a third argument says the order provides for such a purchase.
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(e) the order may provide for a reduction accordingly of the company's capital` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No purchase of shares by the company: outside the scope the paragraph gives itself; not covered.
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(e) the order may provide for a reduction accordingly of the company's capital` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(e) the order may provide for a reduction accordingly of the company's capital` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216(2)(e) the order may provide for a reduction accordingly of the company's capital` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 216(3): the winding up provisions apply`

#ASSERT `s 216(3) the winding up provisions of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 apply as if the order had been made on an application by the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No order for winding up under subsection (2)(f): the "Where" condition fails; the text says no (periods ruling (b)).
#ASSERT `s 216(3) the winding up provisions of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 apply as if the order had been made on an application by the company` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 216(4): further alterations to the constitution`

-- Arguments: an order under s 216 has altered or added to the constitution; the further alteration is inconsistent with the order; the Court has given permission.
-- The bar applies: an order altered the constitution, the further alteration is inconsistent, no permission.
#ASSERT `s 216(4) the subsection bars the company from making the further alteration or addition to the constitution` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No order altered the constitution: "Where an order ... makes any alteration": the bar is not engaged; the text says no.
#ASSERT `s 216(4) the subsection bars the company from making the further alteration or addition to the constitution` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 216(4) the subsection bars the company from making the further alteration or addition to the constitution` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The further alteration is not inconsistent with the order: outside the bar's scope; not covered.
#ASSERT `s 216(4) the subsection bars the company from making the further alteration or addition to the constitution` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Court has given permission: "without the permission of the Court" is the bar's own limit; not covered.
#ASSERT `s 216(4) the subsection bars the company from making the further alteration or addition to the constitution` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The alterations made by the order have the same effect as if made by resolution.
#ASSERT `s 216(4) the alterations or additions made by the order have the same effect as if duly made by resolution of the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(4) the alterations or additions made by the order have the same effect as if duly made by resolution of the company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 216(5): the last day, and failing to comply`

-- The last day is 14 days after the day the order is made; the day of the order is not counted (P1).
#ASSERT `s 216(5) the last day for lodging a copy of the order with the Registrar` (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS Date 15 3 2027
-- Across the end of February in a non-leap year: 20 February 2027 + 14 days = 6 March 2027 (February 2027 has 28 days).
#ASSERT `s 216(5) the last day for lodging a copy of the order with the Registrar` (Date 20 2 2027) EQUALS Date 6 3 2027
-- Across the end of February in a leap year: 25 February 2028 + 14 days = 10 March 2028 (February 2028 has 29 days).
#ASSERT `s 216(5) the last day for lodging a copy of the order with the Registrar` (Date 25 2 2028) EQUALS Date 10 3 2028
-- Across the end of the year: 31 December 2026 + 14 days = 14 January 2027.
#ASSERT `s 216(5) the last day for lodging a copy of the order with the Registrar` (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS Date 14 1 2027

-- Arguments: the person is the applicant; the date the order was made; the copy has been lodged; the date it was lodged; the date the question is asked.
-- Order made 1 March 2027. Lodged on 15 March 2027, the last day: in time; the applicant has not failed.
#ASSERT `s 216(5) the applicant has failed to comply with subsection (5)` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 15 3 2027) (Date 20 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Lodged on 16 March 2027, one day late: failed.
#ASSERT `s 216(5) the applicant has failed to comply with subsection (5)` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 16 3 2027) (Date 20 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Lodged on the day of the order itself: in time (an early act is not a failure).
#ASSERT `s 216(5) the applicant has failed to comply with subsection (5)` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 20 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not lodged, and asked on the last day: the 14 days have not run out; not yet failed.
#ASSERT `s 216(5) the applicant has failed to comply with subsection (5)` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not lodged, and asked on 16 March 2027: failed.
#ASSERT `s 216(5) the applicant has failed to comply with subsection (5)` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 16 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A person who is not the applicant is not bound by the subsection, however late.
#ASSERT `s 216(5) the applicant has failed to comply with subsection (5)` FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 20 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 216(6): the offence and its penalty`

-- Guilty: the applicant did not lodge in time (not lodged, asked after the last day), and lodged late.
#ASSERT `s 216(6) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 16 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216(6) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 16 3 2027) (Date 20 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not guilty: lodged in time; not yet late; not the applicant. An unmet element: JUST FALSE (split site (i)).
#ASSERT `s 216(6) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 15 3 2027) (Date 20 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 216(6) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 216(6) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 20 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The penalty: a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also a default penalty.
#ASSERT `s 216(6) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 16 3 2027) EQUALS JUST (`s 216(6) penalty` OF 1000, TRUE)
-- No penalty is stated for a person the subsection does not make guilty.
#ASSERT `s 216(6) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 15 3 2027) (Date 20 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulative rule s 216(5): the applicant must lodge a copy of the order within 14 days`

-- Time 0 is the day the order is made. The applicant lodges on day 14, the last day: in time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216(5) the applicant must lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar within 14 days` (Member "Ann") AT 0 WITH
    PARTY (Member "Ann") DOES `s 216(5) lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar` AT 14

-- The applicant lodges on the day of the order.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216(5) the applicant must lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar within 14 days` (Member "Ann") AT 0 WITH
    PARTY (Member "Ann") DOES `s 216(5) lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar` AT 0

-- The applicant is a holder of a debenture (a Creditor): the same duty.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216(5) the applicant must lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar within 14 days` (Creditor "Bank") AT 0 WITH
    PARTY (Creditor "Bank") DOES `s 216(5) lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar` AT 10

-- The applicant is the Minister (a declared company under Part 9): the same duty.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 216(5) the applicant must lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar within 14 days` Minister AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Minister DOES `s 216(5) lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar` AT 14

-- BREACH PATH. The applicant lodges on day 15, one day late.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 216(5) the applicant must lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar within 14 days` (Member "Ann") AT 0 WITH
    PARTY (Member "Ann") DOES `s 216(5) lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar` AT 15

-- BREACH PATH. The applicant never lodges and day 15 comes.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 216(5) the applicant must lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar within 14 days` (Member "Ann") AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)

-- Nothing has happened yet: the duty is standing.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216(5) the applicant must lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar within 14 days` (Member "Ann") AT 0 WITH

-- Someone other than the applicant lodges: the applicant's duty is still standing.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216(5) the applicant must lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar within 14 days` (Member "Ann") AT 0 WITH
    PARTY (Member "Bob") DOES `s 216(5) lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar` AT 3

§ `Regulative rule s 216(4): the company must not make a further alteration inconsistent with the order without permission`

-- BREACH PATH. The company makes the forbidden alteration.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 216(4) the company must not make a further alteration to the constitution inconsistent with the order without the permission of the Court` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY (Company "Acme Pte Ltd") DOES `s 216(4) make a further alteration or addition to the constitution inconsistent with the order, without the permission of the Court` AT 3

-- The same alteration with the Court's permission is not the forbidden act: the prohibition is still standing.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216(4) the company must not make a further alteration to the constitution inconsistent with the order without the permission of the Court` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY (Company "Acme Pte Ltd") DOES `s 216(4) make a further alteration or addition to the constitution inconsistent with the order, with the permission of the Court` AT 3

-- No act: the prohibition is standing (no deadline, so it never lapses into FULFILLED).
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 216(4) the company must not make a further alteration to the constitution inconsistent with the order without the permission of the Court` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
